<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>At the moment, I’m still seeing a lot of issues that OCuin pointed out. Most notable is the designation bloat; you have SCP-XXXX-1, SCP-XXXX-A, and SCP-XXXX-2-A through -C without an actual designated SCP-XXXX! I’m sure there are ways to either condense or remove some of these.</p>
<p>In addition, I agree that the ending is currently rather anti-climactic. Your protagonist has barely started resisting, and a small quantitative change like the one you’ve mentioned doesn’t tell us much. What is the reader meant to feel at the end of this?</p>
<p>I’m also not seeing a real purpose for all of the journal entries you have in this at the moment. A lot of the exposition that they provide can be inferred from the logs following them. What would you say they contribute to the narrative?</p>
<p>All in all, I do think you have the foundation of a good article here. You just need to work on what’s built on top of it.</p>
